            <ArticleTitle>Human experimental pain models 2: the cold pressor model.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>165-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-60327-323-7_13</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The cold pressor test is a reliable pain model in which subjects submerge their hands and forearms into ice water while onset to pain, pain intensity, and tolerance are assessed. Although originally developed as a model for hypertension, the paradigm leads to development of reproducible pain responses allowing assessment to analgesic medications. However, analgesic variability to various medications has been observed. A recent study suggests that methodological discrepancies may contribute to such inconsistencies. The model may be more reproducible by utilizing consistent protocols.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
